In DEFAULT mode, the STM8L051F3 starts with a master clock of 16 MHz.
It can be tested by taking it out on Pin 20, Port PC4, CCO pin.
The core operates at 8 MHz, but on the CCO port pin, we can only output the 16 MHz master clock,
which can be divided by a divider located before the CCO output.
If we leave the divider at 1, meaning no division on the CCO, we will measure 16 MHz.
Even if the core operates at 2 MHz or another frequency, the CCO output will represent 16 MHz
divided by the divider placed just before the CCO.
In this program, the CCO output is 16 MHz.
The clock source is an internal RC oscillator of the HSI type in the STM8L051F3.
